ams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Omar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "py", "country_name": "Paraguay", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": 26226, "best_position": 4}, {"artist": "Agust D", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jennie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jimin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jin", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jung Kook", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "RM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "aespa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "j-hope", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "latin": {"genre": "latin", "country_code": "py", "country_name": "Paraguay", "summary": "Latin American music or Latin music encompasses rhythms and styles originated or related to Latin America and its influence in the United States and several European countries such as Spain or Portugal. Some critics have defined Latin music as an incorporation of four elements: music style, geography, cultural background of the artist and language. The first of those encapsulates all music styles generated from Latin countries, such as salsa, merengue.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Omar Courtz", "streams": 105625, "best_position": 5}, {"artist": "Bad Bunny", "streams": 67871, "best_position": 21}, {"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 64515, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "Anuel AA", "streams": 54272, "best_position": 3}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 15395, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Tainy", "streams": 13926, "best_position": 59}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 11958, "best_position": 22}, {"artist": "Feid", "streams": 9712, "best_position": 36}, {"artist": "Daddy Yankee", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Omar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ROSAL\u00cdA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rauw Alejandro", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "py", "country_name": "Paraguay", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KAROL G", "streams": 64515, "best_position": 1}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": 26226, "best_position": 4}, {"artist": "Maluma", "streams": 15395, "best_position": 50}, {"artist": "Tainy", "streams": 13926, "best_position": 59}, {"artist": "J Balvin", "streams": 11958, "best_position": 22}, {"artist": "ABBA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Addison Rae", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Babasonicos", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Beyonc\u00e9", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "post-punk": {"genre": "post-punk", "country_code": "py", "country_name": "Paraguay", "summary": "Post-punk (originally called new musick) is a broad genre of music that emerged in late 1977 in the wake of punk rock. Post-punk musicians departed from punk's fundamental elements and raw simplicity, instead adopting a broader, more experimental approach that encompassed a variety of avant-garde sensibilities and non-rock influences. Inspired by punk's energy and do it yourself ethic but determined to break from rock cliches, artists experimented with styles like funk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Mac DeMarco", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Soda Stereo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Killers", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "psychedelic rock": {"genre": "psychedelic rock", "country_code": "py", "country_name": "Paraguay", "summary": "Psychedelic rock is a subgenre of rock that emerged in the '60s. It is influenced by the psychedelic culture of the time, and psychedelic (psychotropic) drugs, such as LSD and shrooms.\n\nThe musical style often incorporates flowing, hypnotic rhythms. Typical instruments associated with the genre include electric guitar, which is often augmented with effects pedals; various types of organs, which include Hammonds and Farfisas; bass guitar, and drums. Vocals in psychedelic rock music are also sometimes augmented with effects.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Maroon 5", "st